<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Parashurameshvara Temple</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 650</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Parashurameshvara Temple is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> temple dedicated to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiva">Shiva</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhubaneswar">Bhubaneswar</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a>, generally dated to the 7th century. It is one of the oldest and best-preserved temples of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalinga">Kalinga</a> style, with a curved tower and richly carved walls. It is usually attributed to the time of the Shailodbhava dynasty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/parashurameshvara-temple.jpg" alt="Parashurameshvara Temple" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Teamdetourodisha · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Parsurameswara_temple_complex.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
